WHAT THIS NOTICE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

The claim above covers the original work in this repository: the Compose
interface, the session console, the container desktop, the theme and visual
style generators, the preset system and the app's own service layers.

It does not cover the whole tree, because the whole tree is not original work.
The engine is derived from Winlator and from Winlator Ludashi, and parts of the
Steam client layer are derived from Bannerlator. Those are released under the
GNU General Public License, version 3. Other components carry licences of their
own. NOTICE.md records what is in here and where each part came from.


WHY A PRIVATE PROJECT CAN SAY THIS AT ALL

The GPL places no conditions on private use. Its obligations — providing
corresponding source, preserving copyright and licence notices, licensing the
combined work under the same terms — apply when software is *conveyed*: given,
sold, published or otherwise passed to another person. Nothing here is
conveyed. The repository is private and the builds do not leave the developer's
own devices.

So this notice is accurate as long as that stays true, and only as long as that
stays true.


IF THAT EVER CHANGES

Publishing this repository, sharing an APK, or giving a build to anyone else
would make the GPL's terms apply to the result, and this notice would no longer
describe it. At that point the licence for the distributed work would have to be
GPL-3.0, with corresponding source made available and the upstream notices
restored — not because of anything decided here, but because that is the licence
the engine's authors chose and a fork cannot change it.

This is written down so that it is a decision rather than a discovery.
